The table structure information is (table names): 
['sqlite_sequence', 'Player_Attributes', 'Player', 'Match', 'League', 'Country', 'Team', 'Team_Attributes']
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns & how we will use them  

• Match."home_player_1"… "home_player_11", Match."away_player_1"… "away_player_11":  
  – Identify every player that actually appeared (NULL = didn’t play).  

• Match."home_team_goal", Match."away_team_goal":  
  – Decide the result (home‑win, away‑win, draw).  
  – Conditions:  
    – Home win  → "home_team_goal" > "away_team_goal"  
    – Home loss → "home_team_goal" < "away_team_goal" (away win)  
    – Draws     → "home_team_goal" = "away_team_goal"  (omit)  

• Player."player_api_id", Player."player_name":  
  – Translate a player id that appears in Match into a human‑readable name.  

Typical filters / joins we will need  

1. Exclude draws: WHERE "home_team_goal" <> "away_team_goal"  
2. Keep only non‑NULL player slots: WHERE … IS NOT NULL  
3. Connect a player slot to the Player table:  
     ON Player."player_api_id" = Match."home_player_5" (or whichever column)  

Below are 10 exploratory SQL statements (from very simple to the final answer) that would let us inspect the data and finally obtain  

• the player that has been on the pitch the greatest number of times when his team won, and  
• the player that has been on the pitch the greatest number of times when his team lost.  

Each query is preceded by a short comment and returns at most 20 rows.

```sql
-- 1. A glance at some non‑null home‑goalkeeper slots (home_player_1)
SELECT DISTINCT "home_player_1"
FROM "Match"
WHERE "home_player_1" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Translate those player_api_id’s into real names
SELECT DISTINCT p."player_api_id", p."player_name"
FROM "Player"  AS p
JOIN "Match"   AS m
     ON p."player_api_id" = m."home_player_1"
WHERE m."home_player_1" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Inspect a few rows to see the score pattern
SELECT "id", "home_team_goal", "away_team_goal"
FROM   "Match"
WHERE  "home_player_1" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Sample matches where the HOME side definitely won
SELECT "id", "home_team_goal", "away_team_goal"
FROM   "Match"
WHERE  "home_team_goal" > "away_team_goal"
  AND  "home_player_1" IS NOT NULL          -- at least one real player
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. List all players that appeared for a winning HOME side (20 rows)
SELECT DISTINCT p."player_name"
FROM   "Match" AS m
JOIN   "Player" AS p
ON   p."player_api_id" IN (
       m."home_player_1", m."home_player_2", m."home_player_3",
       m."home_player_4", m."home_player_5", m."home_player_6",
       m."home_player_7", m."home_player_8", m."home_player_9",
       m."home_player_10", m."home_player_11"
     )
WHERE  m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Same idea, but UNION both home‑wins and away‑wins so every winning player appears
SELECT DISTINCT p."player_api_id", p."player_name"
FROM (
      -- winners on home teams
      SELECT m."home_player_1"  AS pid FROM "Match" m WHERE m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."home_player_2"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."home_player_3"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."home_player_4"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."home_player_5"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."home_player_6"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."home_player_7"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."home_player_8"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."home_player_9"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."home_player_10" FROM "Match" m WHERE m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."home_player_11" FROM "Match" m WHERE m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal"
      UNION ALL
      -- winners on away teams
      SELECT m."away_player_1"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."away_team_goal" > m."home_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."away_player_2"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."away_team_goal" > m."home_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."away_player_3"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."away_team_goal" > m."home_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."away_player_4"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."away_team_goal" > m."home_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."away_player_5"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."away_team_goal" > m."home_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."away_player_6"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."away_team_goal" > m."home_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."away_player_7"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."away_team_goal" > m."home_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."away_player_8"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."away_team_goal" > m."home_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."away_player_9"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."away_team_goal" > m."home_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."away_player_10" FROM "Match" m WHERE m."away_team_goal" > m."home_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."away_player_11" FROM "Match" m WHERE m."away_team_goal" > m."home_team_goal"
) AS w
JOIN "Player" AS p
ON p."player_api_id" = w.pid
WHERE w.pid IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Count how many WINS each player collected
SELECT p."player_name",
       COUNT(*) AS win_matches
FROM (
      -- every player id that participated in a win
      SELECT m."home_player_1"  AS pid FROM "Match" m WHERE m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."home_player_2"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."home_player_3"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."home_player_4"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."home_player_5"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."home_player_6"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."home_player_7"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."home_player_8"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."home_player_9"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."home_player_10" FROM "Match" m WHERE m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."home_player_11" FROM "Match" m WHERE m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal"
      UNION ALL
      SELECT m."away_player_1"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."away_team_goal" > m."home_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."away_player_2"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."away_team_goal" > m."home_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."away_player_3"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."away_team_goal" > m."home_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."away_player_4"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."away_team_goal" > m."home_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."away_player_5"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."away_team_goal" > m."home_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."away_player_6"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."away_team_goal" > m."home_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."away_player_7"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."away_team_goal" > m."home_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."away_player_8"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."away_team_goal" > m."home_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."away_player_9"  FROM "Match" m WHERE m."away_team_goal" > m."home_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."away_player_10" FROM "Match" m WHERE m."away_team_goal" > m."home_team_goal"
      UNION ALL SELECT m."away_player_11" FROM "Match" m WHERE m."away_team_goal" > m."home_team_goal"
) AS wins
JOIN "Player" AS p
ON p."player_api_id" = wins.pid
WHERE wins.pid IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY wins.pid
ORDER BY win_matches DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

